WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.847 --> 00:00:03.622
Every carton that leaves line 3 must be good.

2
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.815
The module Quality is about how engineers talk about good parts.

3
00:00:09.817 --> 00:00:11.059
You are the engineer.

4
00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:15.290
With the team lead you keep every carton good for a whole shift.

5
00:00:16.323 --> 00:00:18.645
First what is good and how you measure it,

6
00:00:18.819 --> 00:00:22.766
with tolerances and measuring and with variation and capability.

7
00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:26.375
Then watching the process and catching a fault,

8
00:00:26.491 --> 00:00:30.380
with SPC and control charts and with risk and control.

9
00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.288
The first topic is Tolerances and measuring.

10
00:00:34.998 --> 00:00:39.294
The tolerance is how far a dimension may deviate and still work.

11
00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:43.737
The spec limits are the edges of what the customer accepts.

12
00:00:44.438 --> 00:00:46.690
Outside them a carton is nonconforming.

13
00:00:47.698 --> 00:00:49.904
You measure the dimension with a caliper.

14
00:00:51.201 --> 00:00:54.289
The second topic is Variation and capability.

15
00:00:54.996 --> 00:00:57.481
No two cartons are exactly alike.

16
00:00:58.508 --> 00:01:02.362
Capability says whether line 3 can stay within the tolerance.

17
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:05.345
You express that as the Cpk.

18
00:01:06.631 --> 00:01:09.859
The third topic is SPC and control charts.

19
00:01:10.577 --> 00:01:13.120
You see a change before bad cartons appear.

20
00:01:14.126 --> 00:01:16.878
A control chart plots measurements over time,

21
00:01:17.052 --> 00:01:19.664
with a centre line and two control limits.

22
00:01:20.688 --> 00:01:25.367
At the table at the end of the belt you measure a few cartons and write them down.

23
00:01:26.411 --> 00:01:31.206
You plot the average and the range of those cartons on an X-bar and R chart.

24
00:01:32.572 --> 00:01:34.929
The fourth topic is Risk and control.

25
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:38.884
It starts with a bad carton, which must stop moving.

26
00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:42.242
You set it aside in a marked place.

27
00:01:42.938 --> 00:01:44.482
That is called quarantine.

28
00:01:45.507 --> 00:01:48.375
What is wrong you write in a nonconformance report.

29
00:01:49.406 --> 00:01:53.469
That is how you and the team lead keep every carton good, all shift.

30
00:01:54.799 --> 00:01:55.623
The whole map.

31
00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:59.792
The second station is Quality, in Keeping the plant running.

32
00:02:00.808 --> 00:02:03.002
Each of the four topics has four levels.

33
00:02:04.034 --> 00:02:08.550
Start at Basics level with nominal size, tolerance and spec limits.

34
00:02:09.272 --> 00:02:11.014
They are the yardstick for the rest.

35
00:02:12.087 --> 00:02:16.104
At Working knowledge level come calibration, spread against tolerance,

36
00:02:16.301 --> 00:02:18.797
control charts and risks before launch.

37
00:02:19.828 --> 00:02:24.124
At Advanced level come geometric tolerancing, a capability study,

38
00:02:24.425 --> 00:02:26.608
the right chart and the control plan.

39
00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:31.326
At Expert level come tolerance stack-up, the sigma level,

40
00:02:31.466 --> 00:02:33.660
false alarms and the real cause.

41
00:02:34.742 --> 00:02:38.794
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
